{"format":"floorplan/1","building":"CHS","floor":"C","title":"Center for Health Sciences level C (west wings only)","extent":"partial","source":{"publisher":"UCLA Semel Institute (Emergency Action Plan, Attachment B)","what":"UCLA Center for Health Sciences C level evacuation plan (CAD plan of the whole CHS complex, December 18, 2008), page 82 of the Semel Institute Emergency Action Plan (May 2025)","url":"https://space.semel.ucla.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/SEMEL_EAP_5.2025.pdf","file":"https://space.semel.ucla.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/SEMEL_EAP_5.2025.pdf#page=82","date":"December 18, 2008","accessed":"2026-10-15","license":"UCLA document, public on the Semel Institute site"},"how":"Walls are the dark lines of the plan image; rooms are the spaces they enclose, with door gaps closed by extending each wall end up to 2 m. The plan was fitted to the ground with a similarity transform on 6 control points (restroom A4-206 (UCLA GIS), read on the A-level sheet; all four sheets share one frame; restroom A4-208 (UCLA GIS), A-level sheet; restroom AL-217 (UCLA GIS), top of the three small rooms east of corridor AL on the A-level sheet; restroom AL-213 (UCLA GIS), bottom of the three small rooms; restroom 12-250 (UCLA GIS), small room west of corridor 12; restroom 16-293 (UCLA GIS), small room at the top of corridor 16-100).","notes":["The plan is one sheet of the whole CHS complex; only the part inside the mapped outline (OSM relation 331542, the Biomedical Library block and the wings around the two courts) is traced. The four sheets (A, B, C, first floor) share one frame and one scale (scale bar 64 ft = 130 px, 0.15 m/px, matching the fit), so the same control points are used for every level.","Georeferenced on UCLA GIS restrooms that could be found on the sheets: A4-206 and A4-208 (labels readable on the A-level sheet), the three small rooms east of corridor AL that hold AL-213/AL-217, 12-250 and 16-293 (toilet-sized rooms where the GIS points fall; their labels 